  "_readme": "Hand-maintained. The Region facet used to be free text, so one scene minted as many region tags as it had nicknames ('bay-area','the-bay','sf-bay-area','bay' were four feeds). This file is the curated fix: a list of canonical graffiti-scene regions plus an alias map that folds the nicknames onto one slug. BUNDLED into the app (small enough — ~90 regions — that it costs nothing to ship, unlike the ~2.5k-city wall list which is fetched on demand). Keys starting '_' are documentation, not data. `canonicalizeBoard` itself lives in @1nky/protocol; this file only supplies the data. Aliases point straight at a canonical slug; the slugs in 'regions' are the only valid targets.",

